WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.389 --> 00:00:04.929
The last thing we're going to touch upon is just some slides that show off the

2
00:00:04.929 --> 00:00:08.990
different setups you're able to achieve with the Chaos vehicle system depending

3
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:14.250
on your project needs. So the system is flexible enough that it allows you to

4
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.870
set up vehicles with any number of wheels. Just make sure that your

5
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.530
physics asset is set up correctly to account for each wheel and add as

6
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.329
many wheel blueprints as you need to the vehicle blueprint. And

7
00:00:25.329 --> 00:00:29.839
if you want to set up a system where you're towing other vehicles, physics

8
00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:36.640
constraints inside the vehicle blueprint are now much more reliable. The system

9
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.439
also allows for vehicles with less than four wheels. So when it comes to

10
00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:44.979
vehicles like bikes or motorcycles with just two wheels, you'll find that fine

11
00:00:44.979 --> 00:00:48.799
tuning is required to get some more desirable handling. And we've found that

12
00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:52.460
experimenting with the central mass override and rotation damping under the

13
00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.240
torque control settings really helps to stabilize the movement of the vehicle.

14
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:03.090
It also allows for different differential types and accurately simulates the

15
00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:07.209
difference between front wheel and all-wheel drive vehicles. And if

16
00:01:07.209 --> 00:01:11.049
mechanical accuracy of different differential types is important to your

17
00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:14.650
project, you can now have confidence in your setup using Chaos vehicles.

18
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:21.409
Being built from the ground up, the Chaos vehicle system allows for

19
00:01:21.409 --> 00:01:25.370
tackling various types of terrain. And a great feature when combined with

20
00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:29.450
physical materials is to be able to determine the friction of a surface and

21
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:32.849
alter the handling of a vehicle depending on what surface they're driving on.

22
00:01:32.849 --> 00:01:39.329
And lastly, there are a suite of debugging tools that show a visual

23
00:01:39.329 --> 00:01:43.489
representation of what's happening to your car in real time. So you can drive

24
00:01:43.489 --> 00:01:47.450
around your scene and see the forces acting upon the car. And this can help

25
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.450
you track down any bugs with the setup that you have and see the

26
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:54.879
changes you're making when you're tweaking various settings. It's also

27
00:01:54.879 --> 00:01:59.599
important to note that the legacy debug mode still exists, so you can get

28
00:01:59.599 --> 00:02:03.719
on-screen information for things like suspension and friction, as well as

29
00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:08.930
plotting torque data all in real time. So overall, the debugging tool set has

30
00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:09.729
been expanded.
